{"name":"Perfect Landing","hex":"#9eb2c3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"perfect","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Fitting its definition precisely.","Having all of its parts in harmony with a common purpose."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The perfect tense, or a form in that tense.","A perfect score; the achievement of finishing a stage or task with no mistakes."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/perfect"},{"term":"landing","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An arrival at a surface, as of an airplane or any descending object.","An amphibious or airborne invasion."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of land"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/landing"}],"entries":[{"title":"Landing","blocks":[{"text":"Landing is the last part of a flight, where a flying animal, aircraft, or spacecraft returns to the ground. When the flying object returns to water, the process is called alighting, although it is commonly called \"landing\", \"touchdown\"a or \"splashdown\" as well. A normal aircraft flight would include several parts of flight including taxi, takeoff, climb, cruise, descent and landing."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Hawker_Sea_Fury_FB_10_F-AZXJ_OTT_2013_10.jpg/330px-Hawker_Sea_Fury_FB_10_F-AZXJ_OTT_2013_10.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Landing","wikidata":"Q844947"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/PiperPA28CherokeeLanding.jpg/500px-PiperPA28CherokeeLanding.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/PiperPA28CherokeeLanding.jpg/1280px-PiperPA28CherokeeLanding.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/P